OmniHub Streaming Service Database Design and Backend Integration Report

1. Overview and Scope
This design supports a Netflix-style streaming service with:
- Content catalog for movies and TV shows (including episodes)
- User accounts and multi-profile support
- Subscription and payment tracking
- Watch history, favorites/watchlist, ratings/reviews
- Search and recommendation-ready metadata (genre + cast)

Implemented stack:
- MySQL 8+ relational schema
- Node.js/Express backend with JWT authentication
- React frontend login/registration and authenticated favorites/history operations

2. Assumptions
- One account can have multiple profiles.
- Content source IDs come from TMDB (tmdb_id stored as business key).
- Ratings are on a 1.0-5.0 scale.
- Subscription status controls access to watch activity logging.
- Favorites and watchlist are user-scoped.
- TV episodes are tracked by season_number + episode_number.

